Piano specialist model (piano-note.fp16.part1.bin ... part5.bin, joined: piano-note.fp16.onnx)
==========================================================================================

1. Model weights - Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The weights in this file are derived from the checkpoint

  "CRNN_note_F1=0.9677_pedal_F1=0.9186.pth"
  in "High-resolution Piano Transcription with Pedals by Regressing Onsets and Offsets Times"
  by Qiuqiang Kong (Zenodo, 2020-09-17), https://zenodo.org/records/4034264,
  DOI 10.5281/zenodo.4034264
  (the trained model of: Qiuqiang Kong, Bochen Li, Xuchen Song, Yuan Wan, Yuxuan Wang,
  "High-resolution Piano Transcription with Pedals by Regressing Onset and Offset Times",
  IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing, 2021; ByteDance)

licensed under CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
(legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode)

Changes made by Piano2Vision (tests/accuracy/pti_export.py):
  - only the note model is kept (the pedal model of the checkpoint is left out);
  - converted from PyTorch to ONNX (opset 17), input 10 s of 16 kHz audio;
  - weights stored as float16 (cast back to float32 inside the graph), which rounds every
    weight to float16 precision;
  - the STFT's windowed DFT basis is computed inside the graph instead of being stored;
  - the file is split into five consecutive pieces for hosting.
The original checkpoint's authors do not endorse Piano2Vision or this conversion. No warranties
are given; see the licence.

2. Model architecture code - MIT License
---------------------------------------

The network graph was exported from the model definition of the Python package
piano_transcription_inference 0.0.6 (PyPI; https://github.com/qiuqiangkong/piano_transcription_inference;
author Qiuqiang Kong; the package metadata declares "License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License" and the
wheel carries no separate licence file) and its audio front end from torchlibrosa 0.1.0
(https://github.com/qiuqiangkong/torchlibrosa, MIT, Qiuqiang Kong). The training code of the
system is at https://github.com/bytedance/piano_transcription (Apache-2.0 per its README; none of
it is included here).

The note post-processing that turns the model's outputs into notes, src/lib/pianoSpecialist/postprocess.ts
(shipped in the app's JavaScript), is a TypeScript port of the RegressionPostProcessor of
piano_transcription_inference 0.0.6 (utilities.py, piano_vad.py) and is used under the same MIT licence.

Copyright notices: torchlibrosa 0.1.0's LICENSE.md reads "Copyright (c) 2018-2021 Qiuqiang Kong".
piano_transcription_inference 0.0.6 ships no licence file and states no copyright line (its metadata
names the author, Qiuqiang Kong, and the MIT License); the notice below names him as its holder.

